# Company policy — Demo Co

Binding rules for any work produced for this client. QA fails a deliverable that breaks any of
these, and PM must not return work to the client that breaches them.

## Claims and compliance
- No absolute claims: "everything you need", "the best", "guaranteed", "#1".
- No environmental claims ("eco-friendly", "sustainable", "carbon neutral") unless the brief
  supplies specific substantiation. Australian Consumer Law treats unsubstantiated green claims as
  misleading conduct.
- No comparative claims against named competitors.
- Pricing may only appear if the brief states it. Never infer or estimate a price.

## Voice
- Plain English, Melbourne-local. No jargon, no "leverage", no "solutions".
- Second person ("you"), active voice.
- Australian spelling: organise, colour, centre.

## Channel rules
- Google Business Profile: never include a phone number in the body (Google strips or rejects it).
  150–300 characters. CTA from the permitted enum only.
- Instagram: no clickable links in captions — direct to link-in-bio.
- Facebook: do not attach an image to a link post; it suppresses the link-preview card.

## Approvals
- Anything published externally needs human approval first.
- Never claim something is published until a tool has returned a real, fetchable URL.
